                                            "summary":  "Santoli argues that AI has exited its \u0027youthful phase\u0027 and entered a more complicated maturity. The tech sector\u0027s forward P/E has compressed from 29x to 21x over the past year as the market grows unwilling to extrapolate the profit surge without a clear path back to free cash flow generation. The AI narrative has flipped toward risk Ã¢â‚¬â€ regulatory scrutiny, public backlash, and doubts about 2027 semiconductor earnings projections that are heavily dependent on sustained buildout momentum.",
                                            "take":  "This is Santoli\u0027s clearest signal yet that the AI trade has entered a new phase requiring genuine selectivity rather than index-level beta exposure. The P/E compression from 29x to 21x in the tech sector is not trivial Ã¢â‚¬â€ it suggests the market has already partially repriced the risk, but consensus 2027 earnings estimates embedded in sell-side models likely have not caught up. The practical implication: rotate within AI from infrastructure and construction plays toward application-layer companies with near-term monetizable products, where the valuation math is less dependent on extrapolating a capex supercycle that is showing signs of strain.",
                                            "isNew":  true
