                                            "author":  "Michael Santoli",
                                            "url":  "https://www.cnbc.com/2026/09/08/santoli-one-key-tech-etf-may-signal-whether-this-bull-market-can-keep-marching-on.html",
                                            "date":  "2026-09-08",
                                            "imageUrl":  null,
                                            "summary":  "Santoli observes that the S\u0026P 500 preserved its upward trajectory after the summer pullback, reflecting strong institutional sponsorship of equities heading into September. He highlights a dramatic rotation within tech: Nvidia outpaced the broad semiconductor group by 35 percentage points since June 30 after lagging for 11 months, while software recovered 70% of its drawdown. Nvidia\u0027s acquisition of Hugging Face and Meta\u0027s traction with its open-source AI release are cited as catalysts shifting sentiment toward AI consumption plays over AI construction proxies.",
                                            "take":  "The Nvidia-vs.-broad-semis spread Santoli flags is a meaningful signal: when one name accounts for so much outperformance within a sector, it suggests the underlying theme is still narrowing rather than broadening. True bull market health requires the gains to diffuse from picks to the group. The Hugging Face acquisition and Meta\u0027s open-source traction are genuinely important structural tells Ã¢â‚¬â€ if AI monetization is migrating toward distribution and application layers, the investment implication is that picks-and-shovels hardware plays face a ceiling while software and platform names gain relative upside. Watch the SOX-to-SPX ratio as a real-time check on whether this rotation has legs.",
                                            "isNew":  true
