                                                                                "summary":  "Damodaran examines the structural tension at the heart of venture capital: the pressure to scale fast versus the need to build profitable, durable businesses. He argues that current market incentives ÃƒÆ’Ã‚Â¢ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â‚¬Å¡Ã‚Â¬ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã‚Â abundant capital, investor focus on revenue growth, and founder psychology shaped by prior boom cycles ÃƒÆ’Ã‚Â¢ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â‚¬Å¡Ã‚Â¬ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã‚Â have tilted the ecosystem heavily toward growth at all costs, often at the expense of viable business models. The essay questions whether the VC model, in its current form, is generating real value or simply redistributing it.",
