                                                                                "summary":  "Brown profiles Ron Baron, founder of Baron Capital, whose fund has been the top-performing US mutual fund since 2003 by delivering over $60 billion in returns. The core of Baron\u0027s edge is extreme conviction holding ÃƒÆ’Ã‚Â¢ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â‚¬Å¡Ã‚Â¬ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã‚Â he bought Tesla at $14/share in 2014 and still holds a multi-billion position, and has an estimated $25 billion stake in SpaceX. Baron\u0027s philosophy is to identify visionary founders and hold through volatility rather than trading around positions.",
